  result.add "ldScreen.clearPlayerData.title=Delete Player Data from World?\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.clearPlayerData.body1=Select \x22All Player Data\x22 to delete absolutely all player data from the world. The next time any player enters the world, they will start with fresh, default data.\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.clearPlayerData.body2=Selecting \x22Keep Owning Player Data\x22, will retain your current data (such as inventory items & location) and apply it the 'World Owner'. This is any player that loads the world locally or the owner of a Realm it's on.\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.clearPlayerData.all=All Player Data\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.clearPlayerData.allExceptLocal=Keep Owning Player Data\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.clearPlayerData.cancel=Cancel\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.clearPlayerData.progress=Clearing Player Data\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.editor.deleteProject=Delete Project\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.editor.projectOptionsLabel=Project Options\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.editor.delete.confirm=Delete project permanently?\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.editor.deleteWarningFormat=Are you sure you want to delete \x22%s\x22? This project will be lost forever!\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.eduCloud.about.body=Filename: '%1$s'%2$sLast updated: %3$s%4$sTo download, click OK and then click the 'Download' button.%5$s\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.eduCloud.about.title=About Cloud World File\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.eduCloud.delete.confirm=Delete local world?\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.eduCloud.deleteWarningFormat=Are you sure you want to delete \x22%1$s\x22 on this device?%2$sThe cloud version '%3$s' will not be affected and can be re-synced later.\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.eduCloud.resolution.title=Upload now?\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.eduCloud.resolution.body=There was a problem saving \xe2\x80\x9c%1$s\xe2\x80\x9d to the cloud. When exiting a world, please keep Minecraft Education open until the upload completes.%2$sLet\xe2\x80\x99s fix this.\x0d\x0acreateWorldScreen.eduCloud.resolution.uploadNow=