  result.add "ting to '%s'.\x0d\x0apackupgradewarning.manifest_upgraded=This pack manifest has been upgraded to a new version.\x0d\x0apackupgradewarning.duplicate_uuid=Provided UUID '%s' element already exists in pack manifest; Defaulting to '%s'.\x0d\x0apackupgradewarning.multiple_modules=Multiple conflicting modules detected in pack manifest; Defaulting to '%s'.\x0d\x0apack.authors.label=Author: %s\x0d\x0apack.authors.none=Unknown\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.title=Pack Info\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.error=Error\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.info=Info\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.noerror=No errors were found\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.warning=Warning\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.delete=Delete\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.delete.confirm_title=Delete Pack?\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.delete.confirm_body=You are about to delete this resource/behavior pack forever. Are you sure?\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.delete.confirm_delete=Delete\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.delete.confirm_goBack=Go Back\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.packid=Pack ID:\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.packversion=Pack Version:\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.filelocation=File Location:\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.errorlist=Error List\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.file=File:\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.issue=Issue:\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.unkown.packtype=Unknown Pack Type\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.unkown.packtitle=Unknown Pack Name\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.unkown.packdescription=Unknown Pack Description\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.unkown.packid=Unknown Pack ID\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.unkown.packversion=Unknown Pack Version\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.noname=Missing Name\x0d\x0amanifestvalidation.editor.cannotLoadToVanillaWorld=Editor extension packs can only be used on Editor projects. Your world will still load, however we recommend deactivating or deleting the extension packs.\x0d\x0auiPackError.invalidChildNames=%s: Child controls must have unique names: %sIn the future this will be an error and this file won't load.\x0d\x0auiPackError.parseError=%s: Unable to parse UI JSON file with stack: %s\x0d\x0auiPackError.missingControl=%s: Can't find the control: %s\x0d\x0auiPackError.missingControlTarget=%s (%s): Can't find the control '%s' during operation '%s'\x0d\x0auiPackError.missingArrayName=%s (%s): Missing either the field 'array_name' or 'control_name'. \x0d\x0auiPackError.missingCondition=%s (%s): Missing condition on operation '%s'.\x0d\x0auiPackError.missingValue=%s (%s): Missing the value for the operation '%s'.\x0d\x0auiPackError.missingOperation=%s (%s): Missing operation.\x0d\x0auiPackError.invalidOperationName=%s (%s): Invalid operation '%s'.\x0d\x0ajsonValidationError.typeError=%s: Invalid type for property. Expected %s got %s\x0d\x0ajsonValidationError.requiredPropertyError=%s: Could not find required property '%s'\x0d\x0ajsonValidationError.invalidValueError=%s: Did not find valid value for property. Expected %s\x0d\x0aserverUI.errorTitle=Error creating form.\x0d\x0aserverUI.errorDescription=Received invalid form json. Error:%s\x0d\x0acontent.import.failed=Failed to import '%s'\x0d\x0acontent.import.failed.subtitle=See output log for more details\x0d\x0acontent.import.failed.subtitle_duplicate=Duplicate pack detected\x0d\x0acontent.import.failed.subtitle_malformed_zip=Not a valid zip archive\x0d\x0acontent.import.failed.subtitle_premiumcontent=Content in this world is not supported by Minecraft Education.\x0d\x0acontent.import.failed.incompatible=Unsupported file format\x0d\x0acontent.import.failed.title_premiumcontent=Content Not Supported\x0d\x0acontent.import.succeeded=Successfully imported '%s'\x0d\x0acontent.import.succeeded_with_warnings=Successfully imported '%s' with warnings\x0d\x0acontent.import.succeeded_with_warnings.subtitle=Click here for more info\x0d\x0acontent.import.started=Import started...\x0d\x0acontent.import.importedWorldPrefix=imported\x0d\x0acontent.load.failed=Failed to load content for pack %s\x0d\x0acontent.load.failed.subtitle=Check your pack for errors and try importing again\x0d\x0aworldTemplate.festivemashup2016.name=Festive Mash-up 2016\x0d\x0aworldTemplate.redstonemansion.name=Redstone Mansion\x0d\x0aworldTemplate.chinesemythology.name=Chinese Mythology Mash-up\x0d\x0aworldTemplate.GreekMythology.name=Greek Mythology Mash-up\x0d\x0aworldTemplate.Skyrim.name=Skyrim Mash-up\x0d\x0aeduTemplateWorld.theAgentTrials.name=The Agent Trials\x0d\x0aeduTemplateWorld.tutorialWorld.name=Tutorial World\x0d\x0aeduTemplateWorld.mushroomIsland.name=Mushroom Island\x0d\x0aeduTemplateWorld.mooshroomIsland.name=Mushroom Island\x0d\x0aeduTemplateWorld.starterTown.name=Starter Town\x0d\x0aeduTemplateWorld.tutorialVolumeII.name=Tutorial Volume II\x0d\x0aeduTemplateWorld.blocksOfGrass.name=Blocks of Grass\x0d\x0aworldConversionComplete.title=Conversion Complete\x0d\x0aworldConversionComplete.load_prompt=Would you like to play your world now?\x0d\x0aaddServer.add=Done\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.addServer=Add Server\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.addServerTitle=Add Server:\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.addServerDescription=Adding an external server requires knowing the server name and server IP address. Once added, the server can be found in the server list for play.\x0d\x0aaddServer.enterIp=Server Address\x0d\x0aaddServer.enterName=Server Name\x0d\x0aaddServer.hideAddress=Hide Address\x0d\x0aaddServer.resourcePack=Server Resource Packs\x0d\x0aaddServer.resourcePack.disabled=Disabled\x0d\x0aaddServer.resourcePack.enabled=Enabled\x0d\x0aaddServer.resourcePack.prompt=Prompt\x0d\x0aaddServer.title=Edit Server Info\x0d\x0aaddServer.alreadyAdded=This server has already been added\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.header=Add External Server\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.label=Add server by IP/Address.\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.serverAddress=IP/Address\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.serverAddressInput=Server IP or Address\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.serverName=Name\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.serverNameInput=Server Name\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.serverPort=Port\x0d\x0aexternalServerScreen.serverPortInput=Server Port\x0d\x0asurvey.feedbackButton=Send Us Your Feedback\x0d\x0asurvey.label=Select all that apply:\x0d\x0asurvey.line1=Took too long to load\x0d\x0asurvey.line2=Got stuck on an error message\x0d\x0asurvey.line3=Asked too many questions\x0d\x0asurvey.line4=I didn't know it was free\x0d\x0asurvey.line5=I thought I needed a Xbox console\x0d\x0asurvey.line6=Not interested\x0d\x0asurvey.title=Feedback: Why didn't you sign in?\x0d\x0atips.edu.1=You can hold down Shift to take a close up picture using the Camera.\x0d\x0atips.edu.2=Unlike Signs, you can edit Slates, Posters, and Boards over and over again.\x0d\x0atips.edu.3=Use Ctrl+B to turn on text-to-speech capabilities for in-game chat.\x0d\x0atips.edu.4=You can export your Minecraft world to share it with others.\x0d\x0atips.edu.5=To have your peers connect to your world, pause your game and share your join code.\x0d\x0atips.edu.6=Remember that to use slash commands, you need to enable cheats in your world.\x0d\x0atips.edu.7=Done with your creation? Have others tour your world as visitors to protect your work.\x0d\x0atips.edu.8=To code in Minecraft, press \x22C\x22 on your keyboard or touch the Agent icon at the top of your screen.\x0d\x0atips.edu.9=Use the Library to find new game worlds to build in.\x0d\x0atips.edu.10=Looking for a specific biome? Try the Library.\x0d\x0atips.edu.11=NPC stands for Non-Player Character.\x0d\x0atips.edu.12=In Survival Mode, players must find their own resources.\x0d\x0atips.edu.13=In Creative Mode, players can freely choose to build from any of the blocks in Minecraft.\x0d\x0atips.edu.14=Your code building robot helper is called the Agent.\x0d\x0atips.edu.15=Redstone can be used in Minecraft to create circuits and simple machines.\x0d\x0atips.edu.16=You can copy and paste from a text editor to a slate, poster, board, or into chat.\x0d\x0atips.edu.17=Show hints for commonly-used keyboard and mouse controls by pressing \x22H\x22 on your keyboard.\x0d\x0atips.edu.18=You can toggle Auto Jump on or off in the Settings menu under Controls.\x0d\x0atips.edu.19=While in Creative Mode, quickly press jump twice to fly.\x0d\x0atips.edu.20=Choose a Default Game Mode when creating a world to specify the type of gameplay you want.\x0d\x0atips.edu.21=Use the command \x22/setworldspawn\x22 to have new players begin playing where you are standing.\x0d\x0atips.edu.22=Choose a default player permission when creating your world to specify the permissions you want your classmates to have when they join.\x0d\x0atips.edu.23=Press \x22I\x22 on your keyboard or touch the Immersive Reader icon to read or translate in-game text.\x0d\x0atips.edu.24=To add or change an NPC in your world, first make yourself a world builder with \x22/wb\x22.\x0d\x0atips.edu.25=There's a brand new build challenge every month! Find them all in the Library under Monthly Build Challenges.\x0d\x0atips.edu.26=Find related lessons by clicking on tags in the Librar"
  result.add "y.\x0d\x0atips.edu.27=Game moving slowly? Try turning down the render distance in Settings.\x0d\x0atips.edu.28=Want to use Code Builder? Make sure cheats are toggled on.\x0d\x0atips.edu.29=Press F5 to change player perspective.\x0d\x0atips.edu.30=Use \x22/spawnpoint\x22 to change your spawn point. It's just like you slept in a bed!\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.1=Most monsters only come out at night. During the day you're safe... probably.\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.2=Break blocks, pick up resources. Use the crafting grid to make helpful items. Now you're crafting!\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.3=You have endless lives, but your items drop to the ground when you die. Hurry back to pick them up!\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.4=It's a good idea to build a place where you can safely spend the night.\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.5=Use the right tool for the job! Chopping wood with an axe is much faster than using your hands.\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.6=Even in Minecraft you'll get hungry, so try to find something to eat before that happens.\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.7=Digging straight down or straight up might not be a great idea.\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.8=Monsters spawn in the dark. Craft a torch to brighten up any space.\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.9=Beds are great! Craft one to quickly pass the night and set your respawn point.\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.10=Be careful when you swim. Stay under water for too long and you'll run out of air.\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.11=Survival mode has 4 different difficulty levels - Peaceful, Easy, Normal, and Hard. Or play Creative mode and get endless resources!\x0d\x0abeginnerTips.12=The world of Minecraft is endlessly surprising. You'll find lots of different animals, plants, and even \xc2\xa7f\xc2\xa7k\xc2\xa7a\xc2\xa7b\xc2\xa7r \xc2\xa7f\xc2\xa7k\xc2\xa7a\xc2\xa7b\xc2\xa7r\x0d\x0amidgameTips.1=Iron golems will fight for you!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.2=Feed a bone to a wolf to tame it. You can then make it sit or follow you.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.3=Wearing a Carved Pumpkin on your head will keep Endermen from attacking you.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.4=Harvest leather from cows, and use it to make armor and books.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.5=You can fill an empty bucket with water, lava, milk, powdered snow... and even some mobs.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.6=Feeding an animal will keep it from despawning. Build a pen to keep your animals safe.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.7=Get to your destination faster with a minecart and some rails! \x0d\x0amidgameTips.8=Building a portal will allow you to travel to another dimension called the Nether.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.9=Bonemeal (crafted from a skeleton bone) can be used as a fertilizer and can make things grow instantly!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.10=Obsidian is created when water hits a lava source block.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.11=If the source block for water or lava is removed, it will stop the flow completely.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.12=Blocks that can be used as a light source will melt snow and ice. \x0d\x0amidgameTips.13=Take caution when building structures made of wool out in the open, as lightning from thunderstorms can set wool on fire.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.14=A single bucket of lava can be used in a furnace to smelt 100 blocks.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.15=The instrument played by a note block depends on the material beneath it.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.16=Attacking a wolf will cause any wolves nearby to turn hostile and attack you. \x0d\x0amidgameTips.17=Wolves and iron golems won't attack creepers.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.18=Chickens lay an egg every 5 to 10 minutes.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.19=Obsidian can be mined with a diamond pickaxe.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.20=Creepers are the easiest obtainable source of gunpowder.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.21=Tame wolves show their health with the position of their tail. Feed them meat to heal them.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.22=Different colored dyes can be made from a variety of materials, cook cactus in a furnace to get green dye!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.23=Pigs that are struck by lightning become zombified piglins.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.24=Endermen hate bath time!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.25=Sometimes iron golems give flowers to the villager children!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.26=Ocelots show creepers who's boss!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.27=Use seagrass to attract and breed sea turtles.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.28=Protect baby turtles from hostile mobs!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.29=Baby turtles will drop scutes when they grow - these can be crafted into turtle shells.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.30=Brew some water breathing potions for underwater exploration!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.31=Dolphins can lead you to shipwrecks and underwater ruins, feed them cod and follow their trail!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.32=Use shears to carve a pumpkin.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.33=There are 3587 types of tropical fish!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.34=Sea pickles can be smelted into lime green dye.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.35=Use hay bales to breed Llamas!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.36=Compasses always point to the world spawn - craft one to find your way!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.37=Trade with villagers to obtain food, tools, and even explorer maps!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.38=Did you know you can hold a map in your off-hand?\x0d\x0amidgameTips.39=Leads can be used on boats.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.40=Sneak to walk safely on magma blocks.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.41=You can gather cobwebs using shears.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.42=Tridents are dropped by the Drowned, and can be held or thrown.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.43=You can smelt 20 items in a furnace by using a block of dried kelp as fuel.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.44=Taming a skeleton horse doesn't require a saddle.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.45=Phantoms are dangerous mobs that appear during the night. Make sure to sleep regularly!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.46=Zombies turn into drowned if they sink underwater.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.47=Sprint in water to swim!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.48=Be nice to animals!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.49=Don't kill dolphins, you monster!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.50=When digging straight up, place a torch at your feet to break any sand or gravel that could potentially fall down on you.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.51=Shear a Beehive or nest to get Honeycomb, use a Bottle to get honey.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.52=Place a campfire under a beehive or nest to harvest honey.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.53=Emerald ores are the rarest ores in Minecraft! They can only be found in mountains and meadows.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.54=Need diamonds? They get more common as you go deeper.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.55=Frogs eat small and blocky mobs.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.56=The Allay loves to collect items! If you give it a certain item it will try to collect more of it.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.57=Frogs pick a variant based on the temperature of the biome the tadpole grow up in.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.58=You can collect tadpoles in buckets.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.59=Ancient cities can be found under mountain ranges.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.60=Allays love music and therefore interact with noteblocks!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.61=Use a water bottle on a dirt block to get mud!\x0d\x0amidgameTips.62=When wandering in the deep dark, silence is key.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.63=Some animals will follow you if you have wheat in your hand.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.64=Before you mine diamonds, redstone, or gold, make sure you're using an iron or diamond pickaxe or it won't work.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.65=Placing two chests side by side will make one large chest.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.66=Can't find any coal for your torches? Try putting some logs in a furnace.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.67=Infinite wonders, endless possibilities.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.68=Plant some saplings and they'll grow into trees.\x0d\x0amidgameTips.69=Use a hoe to prepare areas of ground for planting.\x0d\x0alategameTips.1=Zombified piglins won't attack you - unless you make them angry.\x0d\x0alategameTips.2=Hit those fireballs back at the Ghast!\x0d\x0alategameTips.3=Cobblestone is resistant to Ghast fireballs, making it useful for guarding portals.\x0d\x0alategameTips.4=Our music is by C418, Lena Raine, Aaron Cherof, and Kumi Tanioka.\x0d\x0alategameTips.5=There will be an update to this game eventually!\x0d\x0alategameTips.6=Creepers were born from a coding bug.\x0d\x0alategameTips.7=The first version of Minecraft was created in just 6 days!\x0d\x0alategameTips.8=The Enderman language is actually English in reverse.\x0d\x0alategameTips.9=The original name for Minecraft was Cave Game.\x0d\x0alategameTips.10=A Spider Jockey is the rare appearance of a spider being ridden by a skeleton!\x0d\x0alategameTips.11=Traveling one block in the Nether is equal to traveling eight blocks in the Overworld.\x0d\x0alategameTips.12=Use phantom membranes to repair your elytra.\x0d\x0alategameTips.13=Elytra can be used to glide, find them in End city ships!\x0d\x0alategameTips.14=Test out some new features by turning on Experimental Gameplay in the settings menu!\x0d\x0alategameTips.15=Monsters that are killed by skeletons arrows have a chance of dropping music discs.\x0d\x0alategameTips.16=Texture pac"
  result.add "ks change the way that blocks, items, and even the menus look in game. Try them out!\x0d\x0alategameTips.17=Using firework rockets boosts elytra speed in mid air. Just... make sure they don't explode, otherwise it'll hurt BADLY!\x0d\x0alategameTips.18=Do people actually read these?\x0d\x0alategameTips.19=Riptide enchantment will propel you through the air in the rain.\x0d\x0alategameTips.20=The Beacon is a powerful item that can only be crafted with a Nether star from the Wither!\x0d\x0alategameTips.21=Nether stars can't be destroyed by explosions.\x0d\x0alategameTips.22=You can barter with piglins.\x0d\x0alategameTips.23=Respawning in the Nether requires a charged respawn anchor.\x0d\x0alategameTips.24=You can charge a respawn anchor with glowstone.\x0d\x0alategameTips.25=You can breed hoglins with crimson fungus, but be careful.\x0d\x0alategameTips.26=Gold is most common in the Nether and in the badlands biome.\x0d\x0alategameTips.27=Diorite, you either love it or hate it.\x0d\x0atips.realms.1=Take a screenshot using the Game menu.\x0d\x0atips.realms.2=A Realm is always online, so you and your friends can play here whenever you want.\x0d\x0atips.realms.3=Keep up to date with what's going on in your Realm by checking the Story Feed in Realms Stories.\x0d\x0atips.realms.4=Share your great moments with the other players on this Realm by adding a story to the Story Feed.\x0d\x0atips.realms.5=Check the Timeline in Realms Stories to find out when others are playing.\x0d\x0atips.realms.6=Access Realms Stories from the game menu while playing on the Realm.\x0d\x0atips.realms.7=Get to know your Realm's community on the Members tab in Realms Stories.\x0d\x0atips.realms.8=Use Realms Stories to get social, keep up with your friends' progress, and organize playtime.\x0d\x0atips.creative.1=Bored of gravity? Jump twice to fly!\x0d\x0atips.creative.2=Summon mobs in an instant with spawn eggs.\x0d\x0atips.creative.3=Collect goat horns and fill the world with music.\x0d\x0atips.creative.4=Combine flint and steel with a TNT block for explosive results.\x0d\x0atips.creative.5=Try blinking around the map with an ender pearl. Don't get dizzy!\x0d\x0atips.creative.6=Use rails and a minecart to build the perfect transport system. Or rollercoaster!\x0d\x0atips.creative.7=Seeking a little more danger? Survival mode has plenty.\x0d\x0atips.creative.8=Crossbows need ammo. Add some arrows to your inventory before going hunting.\x0d\x0atips.creative.9=You can't die, but villagers can. Use that information... wisely.\x0d\x0atips.creative.10=Villagers are great at building villages. Think you can do better?\x0d\x0atips.creative.11=Wolves will attack skeletons to chew on their tasty bones.\x0d\x0atips.creative.12=Tame wild horses by sitting on them until they're calm, then saddle up and ride off. (Note: Horses do not work like that outside of Minecraft.)\x0d\x0atips.creative.13=Eat as much as you want, you'll never get full! And you'll never starve.\x0d\x0atips.creative.14=Move through solid objects using spectator mode.\x0d\x0atips.creative.15=Who needs tools? Punch your way to success and remove blocks instantly in creative mode.\x0d\x0atips.creative.16=Like what you see? Use the pick block button to start building with whatever you're looking at. Yes, even mobs!\x0d\x0atips.creative.17=Get there now with the /tp command.\x0d\x0atips.creative.18=Mobs won't notice you in creative mode, but they'll still notice each other...\xc2\xa0\x0d\x0atips.creative.19=A warden a day keeps the... well, everything away.\xc2\xa0\x0d\x0atips.creative.20=Why not build an underwater base? It's not like you can drown.\xc2\xa0\x0d\x0atips.creative.21=Whatever you can dream, you can build. There's no limit to your resources (in creative mode...).\x0d\x0atips.creative.22=Phantoms can't hurt you, but you can still shoo them off by using a bed. Just...not literally. You sleep in it.\x0d\x0atips.creative.23=Have you tried swimming in lava? It's like sinking into a warm bath. Just don't try it in survival mode...\x0d\x0asplitscreen.joinPrompt=Join as Player %s\x0d\x0asplitscreen.unavailable.toastHeader=Split Screen Is Unavailable\x0d\x0asplitscreen.unavailable.toastMessage=A second player can't join right now.\x0d\x0asplitscreen.unavailable.toastBodyInfo=Tap for more information.\x0d\x0asplitscreen.joyconError.toastHeader=Can't Connect Joy-Con!\x0d\x0asplitscreen.joyconError.toastMessage=You have too many controllers connected while in Local Network Mode to join this game.\x0d\x0ausermanagement.changeUser=Change User\x0d\x0alateJoinScreen.waitingForUserReady=Getting things ready\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.title=Moving files\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.message=Moving \x22%s\x22...\x0d\x0astorage_migration.worlds_error=Some worlds are not available because they could not be moved. Restart Minecraft to try again.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.worlds_error_nospace=Some worlds could not be migrated. You may be out of storage space. Restart Minecraft to try again.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.get_started=Get started\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.retry=Retry\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.go_to_faq=Go to FAQ\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.next=Next\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.resume=Resume\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.continue=Continue\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.start=Start moving files\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.marketplace=Your Marketplace packs\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.main_menu=Go to Main menu\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.faq=Read the FAQ for more info.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.microsoft_store=Go to Microsoft Store\x0d\x0astorage_migration.button.help=Help\x0d\x0astorage_migration.title.initializing=Optimizing data\x0d\x0astorage_migration.gathering_info.description=Gathering information...\x0d\x0astorage_migration.description.out_of_space=You don't have enough free space to move your files to a new location.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.start_transfer.generic.title=New storage location\x0d\x0astorage_migration.start_transfer.description=We need to move your files to a different location on your device.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.start_transfer.total_file_size=Total file size:\x0d\x0astorage_migration.start_transfer.new_location=New location: %s\x0d\x0astorage_migration.resume_transfer.title=Move was interrupted\x0d\x0astorage_migration.resume_transfer.description=We're in the middle of moving your data to a new location on your device. Please press resume to finish the move.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.resume_transfer.description.out_of_space=We're in the middle of moving your data to a new location on your device, but you don't have enough free space.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.resume_transfer.need_to_move=Need to move:\x0d\x0astorage_migration.resume_transfer.available=(%s available)\x0d\x0astorage_migration.resume_transfer.location=Location: %s\x0d\x0astorage_migration.resume_transfer.free_up=Please free up at least %s to continue.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.transfer_error_out_of_space.title=Not enough free space\x0d\x0astorage_migration.transfer_error_out_of_space.files_left=Files left:\x0d\x0astorage_migration.finished.generic.title=All done\x0d\x0astorage_migration.finished.generic.description=Your files have been moved successfully. Please restart Minecraft.\x0d\x0astorage_migration.transfer_error.title=Trouble moving files!\x0d\x0astorage_migration.transfer_error.description=We couldn't move all your files. We encountered the following error: (%s).\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.starting=Starting...\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.gathering=Gathering files from source folder...\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.copying=Copying files...\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.finished=Finished!\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.error.bad_source=Failed (bad source folder)\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.error.bad_destination=Failed (bad destination folder)\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.error.io_error=Failed (file I/O error)\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.error.io_no_space=Failed (file I/O error or no space left)\x0d\x0astorage_migration.progress.error.internal=Failed (internal error)\x0d\x0atrade.doesNotWant=Trader does not want this\x0d\x0atrade.excalamation=!\x0d\x0atrade.expProgress=Experience: %d/%d\x0d\x0atrade.expMax=Experience: MAX\x0d\x0atrade.levelPrefix=Level %d\x0d\x0atrade.levelPrefixAndName=Level %d - %s\x0d\x0atrade.levelPrefixAndName.max=Max Level - %s\x0d\x0atrade.nameAndLevel=%s - %s\x0d\x0atrade.level.1=Novice\x0d\x0atrade.level.2=Apprentice\x0d\x0atrade.level.3=Journeyman\x0d\x0atrade.level.4=Expert\x0d\x0atrade.level.5=Master\x0d\x0atrade.mysteriousText=dab\x0d\x0atrade.notEnough=Not enough %s\x0d\x0atrade.question=?\x0d\x0atrade.trade=Trade\x0d\x0amap.rename=Rename Map\x0d\x0amap.basicMap=Basic Map\x0d\x0amap.locatorMap=Map that Shows Players\x0d\x0amap.extendAndClear=Zoom Out & Clear\x0d\x0amap.clone=Copy Map\x0d\x0amap.name=Map Name\x0d\x0amap.lo"
  result.add "ck=Lock Map\x0d\x0acontentlog.history.title=Content Log History\x0d\x0acontentlog.history.copyToClipboard=Copy to Clipboard\x0d\x0acontentlog.history.clear=Clear\x0d\x0acontentlog.logLocationSectionName=Content Log Location:\x0d\x0acontentlog.settingsSectionName=Content Log Settings\x0d\x0acontentlog.clear_files=Delete Old Logs\x0d\x0acontentlog.delete.title=Delete Old Log Files?\x0d\x0acontentlog.delete.body1=Select \x22Delete Now\x22 to delete all previous log files.\x0d\x0acontentlog.delete.body2=Note: The log file for your currently active session will remain.\x0d\x0acontentlog.delete.delete=Delete Now\x0d\x0acontentlog.delete.cancel=Cancel\x0d\x0acontentlog.delete.progress=Deleting Content Logs\x0d\x0aclient.version.generic=Update %s\x0d\x0aclient.version.1.0=Ender Update (%s)\x0d\x0aclient.version.1.1=Discovery Update (%s)\x0d\x0aclient.version.1.2=Better Together Update (%s)\x0d\x0aclient.version.1.4=Update Aquatic (%s)\x0d\x0aclient.version.1.5=Update Aquatic (%s)\x0d\x0aclient.version.1.11=Village & Pillage (%s)\x0d\x0adr.banner.sale=Sale!\x0d\x0adr.banner.limitedTimeOffer=Limited Time Offer!\x0d\x0adressingRoom.skin_color_picker_title=Skin Color\x0d\x0adr.right_side.category_title=%s\x0d\x0adr.rarity=Rarity\x0d\x0adr.rarity.common=Common\x0d\x0adr.rarity.epic=Epic\x0d\x0adr.rarity.legendary=Legendary\x0d\x0adr.rarity.rare=Rare\x0d\x0adr.rarity.uncommon=Uncommon\x0d\x0akey.emote=Emote\x0d\x0adr.button.ok=Ok\x0d\x0adr.loading=Loading...\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.addition_skin_count=+%s\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.choose_custom_skin=Choose New Skin\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.custom_skin_title=Import Skin\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.custom_skin_description=Import a png (64x32, 64x64, or 128x128) from your device to use as your skin. This will not sync between devices or games.\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.custom_skin_description_disabled=Your device cannot select a custom skin while in a multiplayer game. Please return to the main menu to equip one.\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.custom_skin_description_popup=Players with custom skins will not be visible to you if the \xe2\x80\x9cOnly Allow Trusted Skins\xe2\x80\x9d option is enabled\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.custom_skin_section_title=Owned Skins\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.invalidCustomSkin=Please import a .png file of dimensions 64x64, 64x32, or 128x128\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.owned=Owned\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.purchasable=Get More\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.realms_plus=Realms Plus\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.author_name=by %s\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.author_minecraft=by Minecraft\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.custom_skin=Custom Skin\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.featured_title=Featured & Recommended Skin Packs\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.limited_usage=Limited usage\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.limited_usage.tooltip=This skin can be used here, but may not roam.\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.free_usage=Usable everywhere\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.free_usage.tooltip=This skin will roam wherever you've logged in.\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.purchasing_disclaimer=*Buys %s Minecoins for %s and redeems this pack for %s Minecoins leaving %s left over.\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.skin_count.plural=%s Skins\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.skin_count.singular=%s Skin\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.texture_count.plural=%s Texture Packs\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.texture_count.singular=%s Texture Pack\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.world_count.plural=%s Worlds\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.right_side.world_count.singular=%s World\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.see_pack_in_store=See Pack in Store\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.see_in_store=See in Store\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.realms_plus_button=Realms Plus\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.select_skin=Choose the correct model type for your skin\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.select_skin.title=Skin Type\x0d\x0adr.classic_skins.upsellWithoutStore=You must purchase the skin pack to use that skin, and we c